# Negative-control mutant — isDue / isCancellable (AC-10, ADR-10, design 8.7 [o23])
#
# What this mutant proves: `isDue` and `isCancellable`
# (`contract-product.utils.ts`) still discriminate by invoice status —
# `isDue` no longer reports every invoice as due, and `isCancellable` still
# excludes an `ADJUSTED` invoice (which is due, but not cancellable per the
# legacy `store/modules/data/invoices/index.ts:123-127` set [o23]).
#
# STATUS — landed, structurally sound, currently UNPROVEN. No unit test in
# `contract-product.utils.test.ts` calls either function yet. The shape
# defect that made them unreachable (bare functions mis-shelved on the
# `is*`/`has*`/`can*`-booleans-only meta layer, R23, unexported) is fixed in
# this same commit — both are now exported per-invoice pure functions off
# `index.ts` — but authoring the positive unit coverage is a prover-seat
# task (developer seat writes no test file). Applying this patch today does
# NOT flip a test red; it is filed so the prover's coverage has a named
# target to flip. The prover's AC-10 describe block should assert:
#
#   isDue({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.UNPAID } })     === true
#   isDue({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.ADJUSTED } })   === true
#   isDue({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.OVERDUE } })    === true
#   isDue({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.PAID } })       === false
#   isCancellable({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.UNPAID } })   === true
#   isCancellable({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.OVERDUE } })  === true
#   isCancellable({ status: { code: InvoiceStatus.ADJUSTED } }) === false
#
# Until that block lands, `contract-product.traceability.test.ts`'s
# `SCENARIO_GAPS` correctly keeps AC-10 registered as unproven — this patch
# does not close that registration, only the prover's test does.
#
# Mutation: `isDue` drops its status check and reports every invoice as due;
# `isCancellable` re-admits `ADJUSTED`, which the legacy set excludes.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
